Package: drift
Title: Detecting Riparian and Inland Floodplain Transitions
Version: 0.24.2
Date: 2026-10-17
Authors@R: c(
    person("Allan", "Irvine", , "al@newgraphenvironment.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-3495-2128",
                       affiliation = "New Graph Environment Ltd.")),
    person("New Graph Environment Ltd.", role = c("cph", "fnd"))
    )
Description: Fetch free global land-cover maps (Esri IO LULC, ESA
    WorldCover) or your own classified rasters for any area, such as a
    floodplain, compare them between two dates and across every year of a
    series, and turn the change into maps, tables and change polygons. Fetch dated Sentinel-2
    composites and Esri Wayback imagery to check mapped change against,
    estimate accuracy and error-adjusted area from a stratified reference
    sample, and tag change areas with overlapping records such as fire
    perimeters or cutblocks. Under active development.
